# Base origin for the v2 tier data files (archive/recent/forecast .csv.gz).
# The frontend fetches these DIRECTLY from R2 — reads never hit the Worker. See
# ARCHITECTURE.md ("Reads go direct to R2 / CDN, never through a Worker") and
# frontend/src/services/tieredData.ts (DATA_BASE).
#
# Custom domain on the weather-baseline R2 bucket (zone weatherbaseline.com),
# served through Cloudflare's cache: archive/ is edge-cached (objects carry
# Cache-Control: max-age=86400), recent/forecast are no-store so they're never
# stale. Not a secret (read-only public endpoint). The bucket's r2.dev URL
# (https://pub-403d94ceb15c48af9cb6005b1d541e82.r2.dev) still works as a
# fallback but is rate-limited and uncached — dev-only per Cloudflare.
#
# Set in BOTH dev and prod (committed here): local dev is fully data-remote —
# the frontend reads the tier files straight from R2's public URL, the same
# objects the local Worker (`npm run dev` → `wrangler dev --remote`) writes to.
# There is no local /data route anymore.
VITE_DATA_BASE=https://data.weatherbaseline.com
